      "id": "HDL.4",
      "file": "media/haishinkit/mpeg/MpegTsReader.kt",
      "scope": "class MpegTsReader",
      "op": "insert_after",
      "anchor": "    var delegate: MpegTsReaderDelegate? = null",
      "new": "    fun stop() { videoDecoder?.delegate = null; videoDecoder?.stopRunning(); videoDecoder = null; audioDecoder?.release(); audioDecoder = null }",
      "note": "Swift frees the reader's VideoDecoder (and with it the VTDecompressionSession) and AVAudioConverter when the last reference to the reader goes away, and the decoder's weak delegate becomes nil, so decoded frames still queued for the reader are dropped. Kotlin has no deinit, so owners call stop() at exactly those points: the delegate is cleared, the MediaCodecs are released, the video-decoder HandlerThread quits and the decoder pool is invalidated instead of waiting for GC."
    },
