      "id": "HDL.22",
      "file": "media/rtspclient/RtspTransport.kt",
      "scope": "class RtspTransport",
      "op": "insert_after",
      "anchor": "    var delegate: RtspTransportDelegate? = null",
      "new": "    protected fun deliver(block: RtspTransportDelegate.() -> Unit) { CoroutineScope(rtspClientQueue).launch { delegate?.block() } }",
      "note": "Swift starts the NWConnections on rtspClientQueue, so every delegate call runs there, serialized with start, stop, the timers and the decoder. The sockets block on IO threads here, so each delegate call is dispatched to rtspClientQueue and reads the delegate there. Without this, OPTIONS raced startInternal's requests.clear() (handshake stalled 10 s), RTP decode raced stop and the processor setter, and requests was a map shared between threads."
    },
